From 11bb7bc8bb8c022ca0f861c51440ae45c6756abe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=B3n=20Bjarni=20Bjarnason?= <jon@centroid.is>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:44:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vnc: skip the compositor's own clipboard sources

The clipboard bridge reads every new selection over a pipe. When the
owner of a selection withdraws it, libweston's clipboard.c republishes
the copy it kept as a data source of its own, one with no wl_resource,
and the bridge read that copy too.

clipboard.c serves a send from the compositor's event loop with a
blocking write() of the whole text into the fd it was handed. The pipe
the bridge hands it is drained by that same event loop, so once the
text exceeds the pipe's capacity (64 KiB) the write never returns: the
compositor sits in write() for good, and every client with it. The
process is alive, so docker does not restart it. Seen with a 70 KB
selection; 60 KB got through.

The VNC clients were sent that text when its owner published it, so
there is nothing to read. Skip sources without a wl_resource. In
libweston those are clipboard.c's retained copies and Xwayland's X11
selections, and this compositor runs no Xwayland.
---
 libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c b/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c
index 8ac5c01..176eefa 100644
--- a/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c
@@ -1473,6 +1473,16 @@ vnc_clipboard_selection(struct wl_listener *listener, void *data)
 	if (source->accept == vnc_data_source_accept)
 		return;
 
+	/* No wl_resource: the compositor's own source, which is libweston's
+	 * clipboard.c republishing the copy it kept when the owner withdrew.
+	 * The VNC clients were sent that text when its owner published it,
+	 * and reading it again would hang the compositor: clipboard.c serves
+	 * a send with a blocking write() from this event loop, into a pipe
+	 * that only this event loop drains, so past the pipe's capacity the
+	 * write never returns. */
+	if (!source->resource)
+		return;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_LENGTH(vnc_clipboard_mime_types) && !requested; i++) {
 		char **mime_type;
 
